  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 241 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nThe main weather concern in the long term will be the significantly \ncooler temperatures for the middle of the week. High temperatures \nwill drop nearly 25 degrees from Monday with low temperatures \ndropping nearly 20 degrees. With 850 mb temperatures dropping into \nthe 8 to 12 C range, surface highs will struggle to rise much above \nthe mid 70s on Tuesday with lows dropping into the 50s. These \ntemperatures are nearly 15 to 20 degrees below normals (normal high \nin the upper 80s/low 90s; normal low in the low 60s). These cooler \ntemperatures will be short lived as gradual warming is expected into \nnext weekend. Highs will return to the 90s and low 100s by Sunday. \nOvernight lows will also slowly increase back into the 60s by \nSaturday morning. \n\nAnother round of thunderstorms return on Tuesday evening as a short \nwave trough pushes through Nebraska. Current guidance suggests the \nsevere risk is low as limited to no instability will be around to \nsupport any organized convection. However, we should still get some \ngood rains as areas generally south of Highway 2 could see up to a \nhalf inch or more of QPF. \n\nUpper level ridging and surface high pressure will build back into \nthe region mid-week and outside of some lingering isolated showers \nWednesday morning,conditions will remain dry through the end of the \nweek and into next weekend.",
